{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Before the eyes of all the house of Israel throughout all their journeys.</b> At every journey they would set out, the cloud would rest in the place where they would camp — their camping place too is called a מַסָּע, as in ״וַיֵּלֶךְ לְמַסָּעָיו״ (Genesis 13), and similarly ״אֵלֶּה מַסְעֵי״ (Numbers 33) — because from the camping place they would set out again, therefore all of them are called מַסָּעוֹת."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:57.736283164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}